## DESCRIPTION
## Taylor polynomials
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Taylor polynomials')

################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "parserPopUp.pl", "PGML.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

################################################################
#
#  Setup

$mc_true = PopUp(["?", "True", "False", "Not enough information"], "True");
$mc_not_enough = PopUp(["?", "True", "False", "Not enough information"], "Not enough information");

################################################################
#
#  Text

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` f : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R} `] be [` C^3 `]. Assume its 2nd Taylor polynomial at [` (0,0) `] is given by

>>[` P_2(x,y) = -1 - 3x - 7y + 2x^2 + 3xy + 7y^2 `]<<

For each statement, determine whether it is must be true, whether it must be false, or whether there is not enough information to decide.

[` f(0,0) = P_1(0,0) `] [_]{$mc_true}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \big| f(x,y)-P_1(x,y) \big| = 0 `] [_]{$mc_true}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{f(x,y) - P_1(x,y)}{ ||(x,y)||} = 0 `] [_]{$mc_true}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{f(x,y)}{ ||(x,y)||} =  \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{P_1(x,y)}{ ||(x,y)||} `] [_]{$mc_true}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{f(x,y) - P_2(x,y)}{||(x,y)||} = 0 `] [_]{$mc_true}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{f(x,y) - P_2(x,y)}{||(x,y)||^2} = 0 `] [_]{$mc_true}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{f(x,y) - P_2(x,y)}{||(x,y)||^3} = 0 `] [_]{$mc_not_enough}

[` \lim_{(x,y) \to (0,0)} \dfrac{f(x,y) - P_3(x,y)}{||(x,y)||^3} = 0 `] [_]{$mc_true}
END_PGML

################################################################
#
#  Answers

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
BEGIN_SOLUTION
$BR
There is not enough information to determine whether or not 3.7 is true. The rest are true. Also, note that in 3.4 both limits diverge to \( -\infty \) (recall definition 2.6.16) as both \( f(x,y) \) and \( P_1(x,y) \) are continuous functions with negative value at the origin.
END_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();